A||||2||rc5star||Broken bolts||||8||
Z||000000||rc5star||07-20-2001||11:17 AM||||I have two broken bolts in the lower plenum of my intake. I tried eazy outing them but that didnt work (eazy-out is an oxymoron). I was just going to drill them out and put in a helicoil but I would see if anyone had any suggestions first.  ||||reg||8
Z||000001||StuGood||07-20-2001||11:58 AM||||Do you mean, the two bolts that mount the fuel rail to the lower intake manifold?<P>In a nutshell:<BR>Liquid Wrench.  Spring-loaded center punch.  Step drill until there's only a thin shell of the broken bolt left in the manifold.  Use a pick, a left-handed drill, a left-handed end mill or a tap, to get the thin shell out (using the proper tap).<P>Be glad you didn't break the "Easy-Out."<P>    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||crgkstnr||07-20-2001||01:17 PM||||<P>I had the same problem.  I drilled out the broken bolts on a drill press and was able to save the original threads.  The hole can be opened up to tap drill size (6.8mm) or a bit under if the hole is off center and then try working an 8 mil tap through it.<P>I don't know if there's enough aluminum around the hole to support a heli-coil.<P>The hole could  be "welded up" and retapped.<P>Or  make it a clearance hole  and use a longer bolt  with a nut at the bottom.  This isn't the "right" fix but would work.<P>It would be nice to save the original threads.  Failing that, welding up the hole and retapping.<P>Or getting another lower plenum.<P>Craig<P>||||reg||1
